{
  "paraphrase": "She is the clairvoyant daughter of one of Europe’s longest-reigning monarchs; he is a Californian who calls himself a sixth-generation shaman. Princess Märtha Louise of Norway’s Saturday afternoon wedding to Durek Verrett was no typical royal celebration, yet crowds still gathered along Geiranger’s gray, misty streets to glimpse the bride. The only daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, 52-year-old Märtha Louise is fourth in line to the throne. She and the 49-year-old Verrett wed in a Church of Norway ceremony at the four-star Hotel Union, nestled below the Geiranger fjord, with both royals and celebrities in attendance. Seven bridesmaids accompanied the princess, among them her teenage daughters, Leah and Emma Behn, from her first marriage to the late author Ari Behn, whom she divorced in 2017. About 350 guests attended, including her brother, Crown Prince Haakon, and Crown Princess Mette-Marit; Sweden’s Crown Princess Victoria and Prince Daniel; and the Netherlands’ Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien. Märtha Louise has long charted her own course, once declaring herself a clairvoyant and spending a decade running a healing school that taught communication with angels. In 2022, she announced she would step back from official royal duties to concentrate on her and Verrett’s ventures and to draw a clearer line between their work and Norway’s royal household. On Instagram, Verrett calls himself a “servant of God” and an “energy activator,” and his high-profile clients include Goop founder Gwyneth Paltrow, whom he has described as a “soul sister.”"
}
```

